{
  "id": "fluency-l7-shifted-copy",
  "lesson": "l7-shifted-copy",
  "title": "Fluency: geometric series",
  "n": 20,
  "pass": 0.9,
  "minutes": 10,
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "first-n-terms",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "sum the first n terms of a geometric series",
      "vars": {
        "r": { "pick": [2, 3, -2, -3, 0.5] },
        "k": { "int": [4, 8] },
        "m": { "int": [1, 6] },
        "s": { "pick": [1, -1] }
      },
      "let": {
        "den": "1 + floor(1/abs(r))/2",
        "a": "s*m*den^(k - 1)",
        "t2": "a*r", "t3": "a*r^2", "km": "k - 1",
        "rk": "r^k",
        "sum": "a*(r^k - 1)/(r - 1)",
        "short": "a*(r^(k - 1) - 1)/(r - 1)",
        "flip": "a*(r^k - 1)/(1 - r)"
      },
      "where": ["abs(sum) <= 3000"],
      "prompt": "Find the sum of the first {k} terms of ${a}{t2:+}{t3:+} + \\dots$",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{sum}", "tol": { "abs": 0 }, "placeholder": "A number" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "one-term-short", "value": "{short}", "line": "You used $r^{{{km}}}$, which adds only {km} terms. For {k} terms the power is {k}." },
        { "id": "sign-flipped", "value": "{flip}", "line": "You mixed the two forms of $S_n$. Use $r^n - 1$ over $r - 1$, or $1 - r^n$ over $1 - r$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Here $a = {a}$, $r = {t2} \\div {a:()} = {r}$ and $n = {k}$.",
        "$r^{{{k}}} = {rk:frac}$.",
        "So $S_{{{k}}} = \\dfrac{{{a:()} \\times ({rk:frac} - 1)}}{{{r} - 1}} = {sum}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "up-to-last-term",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "count the terms, then sum",
      "vars": {
        "r": { "pick": [2, 3, 4, 0.5] },
        "k": { "int": [5, 8] },
        "m": { "int": [1, 7] }
      },
      "let": {
        "den": "1 + floor(1/abs(r))/2",
        "a": "m*den^(k - 1)",
        "t2": "a*r", "t3": "a*r^2", "l": "a*r^(k - 1)", "km": "k - 1",
        "lr": "a*r^(k - 1)/a", "rk": "r^k",
        "sum": "a*(r^k - 1)/(r - 1)",
        "short": "a*(r^(k - 1) - 1)/(r - 1)",
        "flip": "a*(r^k - 1)/(1 - r)"
      },
      "where": ["abs(sum) <= 3000"],
      "prompt": "What is ${a}{t2:+}{t3:+} + \\dots {l:+}$?",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{sum}", "tol": { "abs": 0 }, "placeholder": "A number" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "counted-steps", "value": "{short}", "line": "You left out the last term, {l}. The last term is $ar^{{{km}}}$, so there are {k} terms." },
        { "id": "sign-flipped", "value": "{flip}", "line": "You mixed the two forms of $S_n$. Use $r^n - 1$ over $r - 1$, or $1 - r^n$ over $1 - r$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Here $a = {a}$ and $r = {t2} \\div {a:()} = {r}$.", "${l} \\div {a:()} = {lr:frac} = {r:()}^{{{km}}}$, so the last term is $ar^{{{km}}}$ and there are {k} terms.",
        "$r^{{{k}}} = {rk:frac}$.",
        "So the sum is $\\dfrac{{{a:()} \\times ({rk:frac} - 1)}}{{{r} - 1}} = {sum}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sigma-powers",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "sum powers written in sigma notation",
      "vars": {
        "r": { "pick": [2, 3, 4, -2, -3, -4] },
        "b": { "pick": [0, 1, 2] },
        "t": { "int": [4, 10] }
      },
      "let": {
        "cnt": "t - b + 1", "f": "r^b", "rc": "r^(t - b + 1)",
        "sum": "(r^(t + 1) - r^b)/(r - 1)",
        "early": "(r^t - r^b)/(r - 1)",
        "extra": "(r^(t + 2) - r^b)/(r - 1)"
      },
      "where": ["abs(sum) <= 3000"],
      "prompt": "Work out $\\sum_{{k={b}}}^{{{t}}} {r:()}^k$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{sum}", "tol": { "abs": 0 }, "placeholder": "A whole number" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "stopped-early", "value": "{early}", "line": "You stopped one term early. The top limit, $k = {t}$, is included." },
        { "id": "one-term-extra", "value": "{extra}", "line": "You added one term too many. $k$ runs from {b} to {t}, which is {cnt} terms." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "$k$ runs from {b} to {t}: that is {cnt} terms, with first term {f} and ratio {r}.",
        "So the sum is $\\dfrac{{{f} \\times ({r:()}^{{{cnt}}} - 1)}}{{{r} - 1}} = {sum}$."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
